  <!-- Price -->
  <Container id="price">
    <h1>The price of the correction</h1>
    <p class="text">
      Removing the bias is not free. Figure 5 shows the bias rate: the measured
      <Tex src={String.raw`W_2`} /> proxy for ULA follows the exact first-order curve, while MALA sits at
      the Monte Carlo floor. Figure 6 shows the price, in effective samples per gradient evaluation
      and in MALA’s acceptance rate. Switch between the two with the dots above the figure.
    </p>
  </Container>

  <Container width="large" tone="gray" id="fig-price">
    <Slides count={2} labels={['Bias rate', 'Cost']}>
      <div class="slide-content" style="display: block;">
        <img class="fig rounded" src={`${FIG}/fig2_w2_scaling.svg`} width="345" height="238" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="width: 70%;"
          alt="Log-log plot of the zero-mean diagonal-Gaussian 2-Wasserstein proxy against step size h. The exact ULA curve follows a dashed slope-1 reference line at small h and steepens toward the stability limit; the measured ULA proxy follows the exact curve except at the two smallest step sizes, where it sits above it; the measured MALA proxy scatters with no trend in h, at the Monte Carlo floor." />
